# Repository guidance

Read the root `AGENTS.md` for the full project conventions and commands.

## Workspace boundaries

- `apps/backend` and `sites/net.alloydb.console` are Next.js web apps.
- `apps/control-plane` is a Hono service. It has its own database and
  migrations and is not started by `bun run dev`.
- `packages/database` is the shared database for the web apps.
- `packages/site-kit` owns shared site routes. Edit those sources instead of
  generated route shims under `sites/*/src/app`.
- `packages/react-ui`, `packages/core`, and the other `packages/*` directories
  hold reusable web-app code. `packages/control-plane-contract` defines the
  control-plane API contract.

## Imports and app paths

- Use `@/` only for files inside the current app or site.
- Use `@repo/<package>` for shared workspace packages.
- Do not import across app boundaries. Put shared web code in a package.
- Keep the control-plane service database separate from the web-app database.

Use the repository's existing tests, lint, type checks, and package boundaries
when changing code. Follow `AGENTS.md` before running database or deployment
commands.
